
samstat (v2.2.3)

Copyright (C) 2011,2022 Timo Lassmann

Usage: samstat [-options]  <file1> <file2> ....

Options:

   -d/-dir            : Output directory. []
                        NOTE: by default SAMStat will place reports in the same directory as the input files. 
   -p/-peek           : Report stats only on the first <n> sequences. [unlimited]
   -t                 : Number of threads. [4]
                        will only be used when multiple input files are present. 
   --plotend          : Add base and quality plots relative to the read ends. []
   --norm             : Add plots summarising statistics in 1% read length intervals. []
   --seed             : Random number seed. [0]
   --verbose          : Enables verbose output. []

   -h/-help           : Prints help message. []
   -v/-version        : Prints version information. []

Examples:

   samstat ~/tmp/test.bam 
   - will write a QC report to: ~/tmp/test.bam.samstat.html

   samstat ~/tmp/test.bam -p 1000000 -d ~/samstat_reports/
   - will write a QC report based on the top 1000000 sequences to: ~/samstat_reports/test.bam.samstat.html

   samstat ~/tmp/*.bam -p 1000000 -d ~/samstat_reports/
   - will write QC reports for all BAM files in ~/tmp, based on the top 1000000 sequences to: ~/samstat_reports/test.bam.samstat.html

